  "decision": [
    "Keep the representation as a leading experimental candidate: analytical source traces remove much of the difficult contact cancellation without new physics.",
    "No coarser mesh is promoted: principal roll-force discrepancy rises from.201% at20160 triangles to.636% at5040 and.817% at1260. Heave and fixed-cell flux errors are nonmonotone; local metrics are not motion acceptance thresholds.",
    "The independent prescribed-chi solve produces principal heave/roll force errors.132%/.201% and body-potential errors.136%/.218%. The algebraic normal residual is roundoff, but is not the physical validation.",
    "The initial chi is derived from a known external density. Solving for a current density with chi prescribed is NOT a solve at prescribed physical psi; it does not establish correct water/body feedback.",
    "Frozen moment accuracy does not qualify chi_t or eta resolution. Physical dynamic coupling psi_t=chi_t+C*sigma_t must be retained; pressure uses BOTH P*chi_t and Seven*sigma_t.",
    "Fixed-plane even-image zero vertical flux does not apply to a curved free-surface normal. No nonlinear moving-surface promotion follows.",
    "Even sources have a1/r monopole tail unless net density vanishes. Aperiodic analytic C with periodic H must be checked via H*C=2*Simage, zero modes, domain size and volume flux; earlier odd-source conclusions do not transfer.",
    "The final46.44s coarsening CLI is a serial static CPU integration reference, not simulation throughput, an isolated constructor benchmark or a measured realtime speedup."
